  "order": 2,
  "title": "Running, laughing, without breakfast",
  "goal": "Say how you do something with -(y)ArAk and what you do without doing something else with -mAdAn: koşarak, gülerek, kahvaltı yapmadan.",
  "points": ["gp-arak", "gp-madan"],
  "intro": {
    "text": "`-(y)ArAk` says **how**, or **while doing what**: *Koşarak geldi* (She came running), *Müzik dinleyerek çalışıyorum*. `-mAdAn` says **without**: *Kahvaltı yapmadan çıktım* (I left without having breakfast). Like `-(y)IncA`, both leave tense and person to the main verb.",
    "see": "gp-arak"
  },
  "vocab": [
    {
      "tr": "gülmek",
      "en": "to laugh",
      "pos": "verb",
      "card": "fc-0678"
    },
    {
      "tr": "geçirmek",
      "en": "to spend (time)",
      "pos": "verb",
      "card": "fc-0234"
    },
    {
      "tr": "çabuk",
      "en": "quickly, fast; quick (çabuk ol: hurry up)",
      "pos": "adv",
      "card": "fc-0403"
    },
    {
      "tr": "olarak",
      "en": "as (öğretmen olarak: as a teacher)",
      "pos": "postp"
    },
    {
      "tr": "giderek",
      "en": "more and more, gradually",
      "pos": "adv"
    },
    {
      "tr": "severek",
      "en": "gladly, with pleasure",
      "pos": "adv"
    }
  ],
